# Generated dense i18n resolved tables, plus the flat TranslationKey union emitted
# by the same build. These STAY committed (they are the tsc safety net + the runtime
# read source), but each is a machine-emitted artifact regenerated by
# `npm run i18n:build` / `npm run i18n:admin`. Marking them `linguist-generated`
# makes GitHub collapse them in pull-request diffs and excludes them from language
# statistics. Display hygiene only - not removal, not gitignore.
src/ui/i18n.resolved.generated/** linguist-generated
src/admin/i18n.resolved.generated/** linguist-generated
src/ui/i18n.catalog/translation_keys.generated.ts linguist-generated

# pending.ts alone merges with the built-in `union` driver: keep BOTH sides' lines
# instead of raising a conflict. Every PR that adds an English string inserts into the
# same short per-locale list, in all 21 locales, so two concurrent branches collide in
# the same hunk every time. The dense locale slices next to it are large and line-item,
# so their inserts land far apart and already auto-merge; this one does not.
#
# Safe here for one reason: the file is 100% derived and CI regenerates it and diffs
# (the "i18n freshness" gate step over I18N_ARTIFACTS), so a union result that is not
# what the build would emit CANNOT survive CI. Union's own weak spot, an addition
# merged against a deletion (a release fill next to a feature branch), emits a
# duplicate `"<locale>":` key, which fails THREE ways before that: tsc TS1117, biome
# noDuplicateObjectKeys, and the freshness diff. The recovery is the same recipe as a
# manual conflict: re-run `npm run i18n:gen` and commit the regenerated file.
#
# Do NOT widen this to the sibling locale slices. They are read at runtime and are not
# append-only, so a silent line-level union there buys nothing the size of the files
# does not already give, and hides a real disagreement. Pinned by
# tests/gitattributes_merge_policy.test.ts.
src/ui/i18n.resolved.generated/pending.ts merge=union

# Windows batch scripts keep their CRLF endings: exempt from text conversion so an
# LF-normalized checkout (core.autocrlf=input) neither flags nor rewrites them.
*.bat -text
